      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "detangle",
      "prov:value": "The criterion is the owner's, 2026-09-20:",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/guides/detangle.md#provenance-3",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Four roles, because \"one way\" does not mean \"inward\"",
      "prov:value": "`oneWayness` (inbound share) scores **0.0** both for a group with fifty edges\neach way — genuinely tangled — and for one with **zero in and 334 out**, which\nis as one-way as a boundary can be. The owner's clause is *\"arrows mostly one\nway\"*, so the measure must be direction-blind:"
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/guides/detangle.md#provenance-4",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "date",
      "cat-harness:section": "Arrows: is the direction even a fact?",
      "prov:value": "Asked in four words, 2026-09-20: *\"are arrows in wrong direction somewhere?\"*\nMeasured the same hour:",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/guides/detangle.md#provenance-5",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Arrows: is the direction even a fact?",
      "prov:value": "So `role` is now read off **enforced edges alone**, and a boundary made only of\nrecorded ones is `undetermined`. Ten of twenty-two groups are, including both\ngroups whose carve was under discussion. The first cut called them `source`\nwith total confidence on 100% recorded evidence."
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/guides/detangle.md#provenance-6",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Known limits, stated rather than discovered later",
      "prov:value": "- **Four extractors only**: `md-link`, `bpmn-skill`, `json-skill`, `ts-import`.\n  There is deliberately no full-text extractor — a skill that *mentions* another\n  in prose is not depending on it. Under-counting makes a group look cleaner\n  than it is, so the extractor list is printed with the results.\n- **69 dangling references** at the time of writing. A reference to a node\n  outside the scanned set is reported separately and is *not* counted as an\n  outbound edge: counting it would make a group with a broken link look\n  entangled, which is a different finding calling for a different fix.\n- **Only `wrong-direction` is classified mechanically.** `repo-partition.ts`\n  asks the same direction question on the module graph, and since bean\n  `folio-assistant-j79e` both call one function,\n  `cat-harness/schemas/layer-direction.ts`. Here a node's layer is its\n  instance, and what it may reach is its declared `needs` plus itself. The\n  report's `wdir` column counts wrong-direction outbound edges and `undet`\n  counts edges whose source instance declares no `needs` — undetermined, not\n  clean. `restatement` and `essential` stay `unclassified`: they are the\n  adjudication, and `--group` prints each edge's basis so the adjudicator\n  starts from it. The counts are reported, not pinned — the sidecar ruling\n  pins size, cohesion and authority counts only.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean folio-assistant-j79e"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/guides/detangle.md#provenance-7",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "For agents working on detangle",
      "prov:value": "This section was the instance's `AGENTS.md`, moved here unchanged when the instance was folded."
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/guides/detangle.md#provenance-8",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "What the graph actually looks like",
      "prov:value": "## What the graph actually looks like\n\nMeasured 2026-09-20, 443 nodes and 758 edges:\n\n| group | size | in | out | groups | dir | role |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `skills/folio-core` | 108 | **254** | 10 | 3 | 0.92 | sink |\n| `skills/authoring/content-lifecycle` | 10 | 88 | 1 | 1 | 0.98 | sink |\n| the DAK layer's `skills/content/authoring-who-smart-guidelines` | 11 | 60 | 0 | 0 | 1.00 | sink |\n| `cat-harness/schemas` | 132 | 5 | 1 | 1 | 0.67 | sink |\n| `processes` | 41 | **0** | **334** | 6 | 1.00 | **source** |\n| `scenarios` | 1 | 0 | 122 | 6 | 1.00 | source |\n| `skills/memory` | 37 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 1.00 | isolated |\n| the science layer's `skills/content/folio-paper-adapter` | 66 | 47 | 16 | 2 | **0.49** | **tangled** |\n\n**Two tangled groups out of twenty-two.** This is a well-layered graph, and the\nlayering is the one the architecture describes: skill packages are leaves,\norchestration (`workflows`, `roles`, `tools`) is the root. Only\n`folio-paper-adapter` and `bootstrap/skills` are genuinely entangled.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/guides/detangle.md#provenance-9",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Two defects this found in its own first cut",
      "prov:value": "## Two defects this found in its own first cut\n\nBoth were in the measurement, not the graph, and both are recorded because a\nnumber nobody can re-derive is a number nobody can argue with.\n\n1. **Name collision in resolution.** Five `<bootstrap.processes:skill ref>` values —\n   `activity-log`, `getting-started`, `l2-dak-authoring`, `qa-report-signing`,\n   `upstream-version-adoption` — are *also* basenames of diagrams in the same\n   directory. Preferring a same-group hit resolved every one to the diagram\n   referring to it. That manufactured **31 phantom internal edges and all 8\n   reported inbound edges** for `processes`. A skill ref names a skill;\n   the resolver is now restricted by extension.\n2. **Missing call edges.** `<bpmn:import>`, `calledElement` and `decisionRef`\n   were not extracted at all — 39 edges, and they are precisely the *internal*\n   edges of a workflow graph. Cohesion for the group under discussion was\n   understated for the whole time its carve was being argued.\n\nAfter both fixes `processes` reads **0 in / 334 out**, not 8 / 303. The\nconclusion held; the evidence for it did not."
    }
  ]
